      "kind": "text",
      "lineHeight": 1.5,
      "size": 11.5,
      "text": "At the ferry a man was mending a net with slow, patient fingers. He did not look up when she asked about the evening crossing; he only nodded toward the water, where a small lamp was already burning on the far bank.",
      "tracking": 0
